  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with scvi_n200 + multiprofile + transformer (config_006, acc 0.653) is the clear best so far, and image-only with resnet50 is very weak (config_010, acc 0.208). The aggregation choice (avgpool vs transformer) shows negligible difference, and scgpt/pca are clearly inferior to scvi_n200. The major unexplored question is whether adding image features provides complementary signal on top of the strong RNA representation. This experiment (config_032) takes the best RNA configuration and adds resnet50 image features with concat fusion, isolating the effect of multimodal fusion while holding all other design choices at their best-known values. It is the minimal, controlled extension of our current best: if accuracy exceeds 0.653, image adds value and we should explore ViT and weighted fusion; if it does not, we know resnet50 image features are not complementary and should pivot to testing imagenet_vit_l in a multimodal setting. This is the highest-information single experiment under the budget because it directly answers whether the multimodal direction is worth further investment."
}

